  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\rPlans\rE00\rP00\rP01\rP02\rP03\rP04\rP05\rP06\rP07\rFlood Risk Assessment\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the HMO, Cycle parking, shall be provided as indicated on drawing P01, in accordance with the following requirements:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces;\r\r- in an accessible location; the store door must have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\r\r- long stay cycle parking spaces secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\r- fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area\r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development, the refuse storage facilities shown on drawing number P01 shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Borough's waste reduction targets.\r\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r\r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area\r\r",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown on drawings P01 and P02, prior to commencement of the development, a revised ground floor plan showing the communal kitchen/dining room laid out with the dining area positioned nearer to the internal exit door than the kitchen and cooking facilities shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved layout shall be implemented prior to first occupation of the HMO and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory means of escape and a good quality communal kitchen/dining area for future occupiers, in accordance with Policies DMD5 and DMD8 and the Council's HMO Standards.\r"
  ],
